Terms and Conditions - micro syntax rules and colour scheme
===========================================================

bunmsh does not bundle any file from micro, the Go terminal editor at
https://github.com/zyedidia/micro. What it derives from micro is:

  * The shell-syntax highlighting rules `pspac` applies to the COMMAND column
    of its process listing. The patterns and word lists of micro's
    `runtime/syntax/sh.yaml` — keywords, command names, flags, variables,
    strings, comments — and the order they resolve in were transcribed into
    `src/shell.js`.

  * The colours those classes are painted in, which are the colour-links of
    micro's `runtime/colorschemes/monokai.micro`, transcribed into the same
    file. `src/cat-fancy.js` takes five of the same colour-links for the
    JSON it colours.

Both come from micro's own tree — `runtime/syntax/sh.yaml` and
`runtime/colorschemes/monokai.micro` — and that is where to trace this
licence from: `runtime/syntax/LICENSE` and `LICENSE` in
https://github.com/zyedidia/micro.

